t down and spread out. We went a little bit further along to tighten it up.</div><div class="timestamp">28:44</div><div class="transcript-line">So now we&#39;re up here a little bit. We kind of second platoon is now protect them. Uh that&#39;s my job is to protect the headquarters uh this platoon they should have been.</div><div class="timestamp">29:04</div><div class="transcript-line">They are kinda out there like that now And this connecting file is still a file. Keep track of what&#39;s going on with alpha. At about 10 o&#39;clock, 10.</div><div class="timestamp">29:19</div><div class="transcript-line">56 1055 1005 depending on which brigade log you look at but about 10 o&#39;clock just all hell broke loose and that was uh uh uh primarily this battalion tried to shoot at these guys I understand and they&#39;re in bunkers. Some were built for the Japanese, some were built for the French. They&#39;re all bunkers.</div><div class="timestamp">29:51</div><div class="transcript-line">So uh tunnels underground 20 40 20 to 40 feet deep. So if you were getting a lot of good shots at Americans, you had the battalion that&#39;s about two, three You had everybody running up here and uh sticking their heads up and shooting at the Americans and then running running back in the bunker, getting more ammunition. So they all shot.</div><div class="timestamp">30:16</div><div class="transcript-line">In the original fire, a few people shot at us. One guy shot and hit Captain Blackwell. The Captain Blackwell was the first one of my guys hit.</div><div class="speaker">Andrew Woods</div><div class="timestamp">30:26</div><div class="transcript-line">He&#39;s the S2?</div><div class="speaker">Clark Welch</div><div class="timestamp">30:28</div><div class="transcript-line">The S2. What the hell was he doing out there? Yeah, Captain Blackwell he has too.</div><div class="timestamp">30:33</div><div class="transcript-line">He had told me a couple days before that he I would see him a lot because his real job was to be ready to take over D Company when I became a casualty And uh I say, well, good luck, you know, I&#39;m not going to become a casualty screw ya. But Captain Blackwell, a couple of times before had walked with me. He never said anything.</div><div class="timestamp">30:57</div><div class="transcript-line">He he was a good man. Very smart. He just walked along with me.</div><div class="timestamp">31:02</div><div class="transcript-line">But he told me, so I&#39;ll know what to do. so I can take over when you become a captain. And we received a few shots.</div><div class="timestamp">31:09</div><div class="transcript-line">And we received a few shots from guys that were in trees. Made people think there&#39;s snipers in the trees. Not really.</div><div class="timestamp">31:16</div><div class="transcript-line">Just a guy&#39;s up in the tree with a radio and he&#39;s got a rifle and he sees Americans so he shoots them. So some of these guys were shooting at us. But most of the fire was coming from right there.</div><div class="timestamp">31:29</div><div class="transcript-line">Five meters away, ten meters away. If you got much more than ten meters away, you couldn&#39;t see. Now, when a big fight starts, they had 57 millimeter recoilish rifles.</div><div class="timestamp">31:42</div><div class="transcript-line">That&#39;s a that&#39;s a you don&#39;t blow up a tank. They were shooting those at us. They had 50 caliber machine guns, those captured from us, and also the ones they hit on the tripods because he had an anti-aircraft company.</div><div class="timestamp">31:55</div><div class="transcript-line">with him. They had 50 calibers mounted on tripods. But so you just turn them down so it means 50 calibers are coming through about that high.</div><div class="timestamp">32:05</div><div class="transcript-line">Tremendous amount of fire on Alpha Company, a little bit of fire on us. And uh my primary job was to keep them getting my guys down and And uh Carlin Allen said, Well what&#39;s what&#39;s happened to Alpha Company? get him on the radio.</div><div class="timestamp">32:30</div><div class="transcript-line">And uh he either told me to go up there, I said I&#39;ll go up there. I&#39;d already been up with uh this is uh Stroop. Ted.</div><div class="timestamp">32:43</div><div class="transcript-line">Stroop, I just forgot his first name. Dave. Dave.</div><div class="timestamp">32:46</div><div class="transcript-line">Lieutenant Stroop is up here. I ran up to the front And uh what I saw when I got there with Stroop, I said, what the hell? And Stroop said, they&#39;re gone.</div><div class="timestamp">33:00</div><div class="transcript-line">And what I saw, what I saw, was a body laying there, body laying there, body laying there, body laying there, body laying there, body laying there. And I ran up there, I don&#39;t know how far I went. But I saw 10 to 20 bodies laying on the ground.</div><div class="timestamp">33:22</div><div class="transcript-line">I picked up one or two of the guys that were wounded. When I say bodies, I couldn&#39;t tell. if they&#39;re alive or dead.</div><div class="timestamp">33:28</div><div class="transcript-line">They&#39;re just soaking wet and they&#39;re laying on the ground. I saw those guys laying on the ground. I didn&#39;t see see anything else.</div><div class="timestamp">33:40</div><div class="transcript-line">I don&#39;t know. I mean I personally do not know what Alpha Company did. I do know they weren&#39;t there.</div><div class="timestamp">33:48</div><div class="transcript-line">Now from their own reports later on that they they ran back here. And back here is that draw that we showed on the other thing. The draw is kind of kind of a dry creek bed and uh the woods comes down like that.</div><div class="timestamp">34:11</div><div class="transcript-line">It&#39;s all heavy woods. Yeah. I do know that I I could see, I could talk to no one from Alpha Company.</div><div class="timestamp">34:23</div><div class="transcript-line">There&#39;s a tremendous amount of fire coming. Coming in from the right. None hit me then.</div><div class="timestamp">34:28</div><div class="transcript-line">Yes, one hit me in the leg. Lieutenant Stroop came up with me. My two radio operators came up with me We picked up two or three of the bodies, dead or alive.</div><div class="timestamp">34:39</div><div class="transcript-line">We picked up an armload of weapons, some ammunition, and came right and back and I came back to see Colonel Allen said sir alpha company&#39;s gone no alpha company up there And uh throughout the next couple hours, Colonel Allen would ask me, where&#39;s Alpha Company? So I told you, there&#39;s nobody up there. Now, Ted Stave Stroop, uh, eventually I came up there with my uh Ford Observer.</div><div class="timestamp">35:13</div><div class="transcript-line">Dave Stroop made some other trips in there and brought back some living or dead guys uh brought back a lot of weapons and an awful lot of ammunition. We did not run out of ammunition that day. We had plenty of ammunition and we had plenty of weapons.</div><div class="timestamp">35:32</div><div class="transcript-line">I was carrying M16 when it got shot. Just get another one. Now, Alpha Company&#39;s gone.</div><div class="timestamp">35:42</div><div class="transcript-line">I&#39;m in a tight circle. I expected a lot of alpha company people to come back to me, but just a very, very few did. I just didn&#39;t see off company anymore.</div><div class="timestamp">35:52</div><div class="transcript-line">So that now I noticed that most of the fire came from that side, and then the fire from them just kept pick picking up. And pretty soon it was just a they were shooting at me because there wasn&#39;t anybody else to shoot at down here. The ones down there are already dead.</div><div class="timestamp">36:12</div><div class="transcript-line">Tremendous fire. Then, as Colonel Triette told me, he 