he shooting started, up to the time the shooting started, I wasn&#39;t allowed to fire anything.</div><div class="timestamp">38:17</div><div class="transcript-line">The first Indian Division SOP, standard operating procedure, said that only the lead company can fire, which makes sense. If I&#39;d been firing also, maybe I would have fired up the lead company, so the lead company fires the trail company is just ready to do whatever they&#39;re supposed to do. I had planned for fire.</div><div class="timestamp">38:39</div><div class="transcript-line">All of along everywhere, left and right, front, back. But I couldn&#39;t shoot it. But I was calling back to there are two kinds of indirect fire that I get.</div><div class="timestamp">38:47</div><div class="transcript-line">I call back to the mortars. Calk directly to him and say, okay, if I were allowed to shoot, I would now want you to shoot Alpha 1. And he&#39;d say, Roger.</div><div class="timestamp">39:01</div><div class="transcript-line">And I guess they aimed the guns towards Alpha 1. And then when I got up here, I would say, if I were allowed to shoot, I&#39;d now want to shoot Alpha 2. So it moves the guns a little bit.</div><div class="timestamp">39:12</div><div class="transcript-line">And so that&#39;s right there, but nothing&#39;s being shot, but we&#39;re talking about now you&#39;d shoot alpha one, now you&#39;d shoot alpha two. come back then he can talk more about the mortars. The artillery&#39;s the same way.</div><div class="timestamp">39:26</div><div class="transcript-line">We had artillery over here that we used on the 16th in Shantan, very, very well on the 16th. We had other artillery. I didn&#39;t care where it came from.</div><div class="timestamp">39:35</div><div class="transcript-line">I just knew I wanted Pinky Durham to be able to get on the phone and get it. On the 16th, we had tremendous amount of artillery and mortars. They fired.</div><div class="timestamp">39:43</div><div class="transcr