onged bullshit first to last.</div><div class="timestamp">01:42:42</div><div class="transcript-line">Uh that is him uh conducting an unexpected attack on a Temporary or halted enemy, so it is an ambush. But he didn&#39;t set up an ambush.</div><div class="speaker">Andrew Woods</div><div class="timestamp">01:43:01</div><div class="transcript-line">Over a hundred lost.</div><div class="speaker">Clark Welch</div><div class="timestamp">01:43:06</div><div class="transcript-line">I did ask him and you asked me on the phone, uh how many casual you know, I said uh I I lost a lot. I lost hundred and forty two people. He said, I&#39;m sorry.</div><div class="timestamp">01:43:15</div><div class="transcript-line">I said, how many did you lose? And the this was in the meeting room back at the uh big government place the day before we went out there to together. He was on his side of the table and I was on my side.</div><div class="timestamp">01:43:28</div><div class="transcript-line">And when I said, how many did you lose? the handlers behind him, about six. The chief of the Office of Public Affairs, all the communist handlers and interpreters.</div><div class="timestamp">01:43:40</div><div class="transcript-line">Said, no numbers, no numbers, no numbers. There&#39;s a word for number, I remember what it is. But Kong Kong no uh whatever it is.</div><div class="timestamp">01:43:47</div><div class="transcript-line">No numbers, no numbers, no numbers. And Colonel Tripp. And okay, no numbers.</div><div class="timestamp">01:43:54</div><div class="transcript-line">And then the next day we&#39;re out in the field. I said, how many did you lose? said a company about a company.</div><div class="timestamp">01:44:03</div><div class="transcript-line">And then he said again, you know, if if you were wounded, you died. And if he left them behind, he never did pick them up again. So he left behind 60 to 100 people.</div><div class="timestamp">01:44:18</div><div class="transcript-line">fair exchange. But he did he hid 60 to 100 casualties. And that&#39;s because he told me I lost a company.</div><div class="timestamp">01:44:30</div><div class="transcript-line">And he told me he lost a platoon earlier out here on the 16th. He lost a platoon and he lost a company here. And as we talked about casualties, and I said Or something.</div><div class="timestamp">01:44:46</div><div class="transcript-line">And he said, well, you know, we didn&#39;t lose many to artillery and air, which is your strength. Because we grab you by the belt buckle so close to you. And then he said uh that&#39;s it that&#39;s twice.</div><div class="timestamp">01:45:03</div><div class="transcript-line">He said it once to uh consoy And I was standing with Gunzoiler. And he said it once to me, we were together in the van. He said, on that day, no one won.</div><div class="timestamp">01:45:13</div><div class="transcript-line">And then the other thing he said, I was going to tell you. He said, don&#39;t feel bad about that. You saved my life.</div><div class="timestamp">01:45:20</div><div class="transcript-line">What do you mean I saved your life? Shit, I would have killed you if I&#39;d seen you. I tried to kill you.</div><div class="timestamp">01:45:25</div><div class="transcript-line">Never killed you. saw you. He said, no, you saved my life.</div><div class="timestamp">01:45:28</div><div class="transcript-line">He said, my job was to go from here when he was over here on the other side of Highway 13. in War Zone D. My job was to go through the long wait he didn&#39;t call them long wind zone. He didn&#39;t even call it North Southeast.</div><div class="timestamp">01:45:43</div><div class="transcript-line">Vietnam, it&#39;s Vietnam. My job was to go from here across here to the vicinity of Nui Ba Den, a big mountain bare rock just sticking up. The center of New Eva Den and then turn over and come back up this way to uh locked in.</div><div class="timestamp">01:46:00</div><div class="transcr